{
  "biological_interpretation": "Lowering either ATXN10 or EEF1A2 exposes a restricted neuronal communication and cytoskeletal vulnerability rather than a generic ataxia-network or translation-elongation signature across all neurons.",
  "caveats": [
    "SCA10 is usually modeled as a toxic intronic repeat RNA disease; the atlas tested total Atxn10 lowering.",
    "The Atxn10/Eef1a2 relationship is convergence at selected markers, not a strong whole-transcriptome phenocopy."
  ],
